@node GettingStarted "Getting started"
@toc Main
@next Format

The default language guide is staged by @{b}gmake guides@{ub} both next to the
program (PROGDIR:) and under HELP:. The Makefile's run scripts assign HELP: to
DEV:Help so FS-UAE finds it. src/help.c opens the current node on the app's own
screen.

Next: @{" AmigaGuide format " link Format}
@endnode

@node Format "AmigaGuide format"
@toc Main
@prev GettingStarted

A guide is plain text. A @{b}@@@{ub} in column 0 starts a command; @{b}@@{...}@{ub}
in body text is an inline attribute.

    @{b}@@node name "title"@{ub}   start a node (link target + window title)
    @{b}@@endnode@{ub}            end the node
    @{b}@@{b} ... @@{ub}@{ub}     bold on / off
    @{b}@@{i} ... @@{ui}@{ub}     italic on / off
    @{b}@@{"text" link node}@{ub} a clickable link to another node

See @docs/amigaguide-format.md for the full digest.
@endnode
